---
layout: layouts/site.njk
permalink: /growth-roadmap/
title: "Free Growth Roadmap for DTC Brands | Freeland"
description: "A free marketing audit for DTC brands. Kevin Freeland starts from your public store and ads plus five answers. You keep the roadmap either way."
heroPreload: /images/ns-dawn-boxes.avif
faqKey: roadmap
pageScripts: ["/js/apply.js"]
breadcrumbs:
  - { name: "Home", url: "/" }
  - { name: "Growth Roadmap", url: "/growth-roadmap/" }
schema:
  - "@type": "Service"
    "@id": "https://freelandme.com/growth-roadmap/#service"
    name: "Growth Roadmap"
    provider: { "@id": "https://freelandme.com/#org" }
    areaServed: "US"
    description: "A free, plain-English read of a DTC brand's ads, landing page and checkout, offer, retention and tracking. Kevin starts from what is public plus the five application answers. A deeper read needs account access, agreed on the call. Kevin walks the brand owner through it on a 30-minute call, and the brand keeps it either way."
---
{% from "partials/reviews.njk" import reviews %}
<section class="hero hero-short" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <picture class="hero-media">
    <source type="image/avif" srcset="/images/ns-dawn-boxes.avif">
    <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/ns-dawn-boxes.webp">
    <img src="/images/ns-dawn-boxes.jpg" alt="Packed shipping boxes on a steel table at dawn" width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high">
  </picture>
  <div class="wrap hero-content">
    <h1 id="hero-title"><span>See where your brand</span> <span>is leaking money.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Kevin starts from your public store and ads plus five answers, then puts the leaks in order. Free, and yours to keep.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="#apply" data-cta="roadmap_hero_apply">Get your Growth Roadmap</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="#example" data-cta="roadmap_hero_example">See an example</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="get-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-head">
      <h2 id="get-title">What you get</h2>
      <p>Five areas, read by a person. Kevin starts from what is public plus your answers. A deeper read of your accounts needs view access, agreed on the call. On a 30-minute call he walks you through it in plain English, in order, with where to start.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="rows">
      <li>
        <h3>Paid ads</h3>
        <p>Your ads on Meta, Google, Bing and TikTok, starting from what is public. With view access, the campaigns themselves: where money looks wasted and which winners are held back.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Landing page and checkout</h3>
        <p>Whether the page a buyer lands on matches what the cart charges, and where buyers drop between the two.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Offer and subscription</h3>
        <p>How the offer is built, what is selected by default, and what a first order turns into over time.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Retention and email</h3>
        <p>What happens after the first order: the flows that run, the ones that are missing, and the buyers who never hear from you again.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Tracking</h3>
        <p>Whether the numbers you steer by can be trusted. If the tracking is off, decisions built on it are off too. Kevin checks this once you give view-only access, agreed on the call.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" id="example" aria-labelledby="example-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="example-title">What a roadmap looks like</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:22px">Each leak comes with its fix. Here are four common ones.</p>
    <figure class="sample reveal sequence" style="margin-top:48px">
      <figcaption>
        <span class="sample-title">Growth Roadmap</span>
        <span class="sample-note">An example. Your roadmap uses your own store.</span>
      </figcaption>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">The leak</th><th scope="col">The fix</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Ads send buyers to a price the cart does not honor.</th>
            <td>One price everywhere, checked against the real checkout before any money is spent.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Winning ads stall because nobody raises them.</th>
            <td>Budgets go up on a set rule while an ad keeps selling.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Subscribe-and-save is not the default.</th>
            <td>Pre-select it, and keep one-time one tap away.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">The sale ends on the site but not in the ads.</th>
            <td>Date-gate the banner, pages and ads together, so they change on the same schedule.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="sample-foot">Your roadmap starts from your public store and ads plus your answers. With view access, it uses your own numbers.</p>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="keep-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <h2 id="keep-title" class="split-head">You keep it whether or not you hire us.</h2>
    <div class="body-copy">
      <p class="lede">The roadmap is yours. Hand it to your team, your agency or nobody.</p>
      <p>After Kevin walks you through it on the call, you decide whether you want us to do the work or to do it yourself. Either way, you have a list of what to fix first.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="fit-title">Who it is not for</h2>
    <div class="fit" style="margin-top:48px">
      <div class="fit-no">
        <h3>Not for</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Pre-launch ideas with nothing selling yet</li>
          <li>Brands looking for the cheapest vendor</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Built for</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Founder-led DTC brands already selling online</li>
          <li>Founders who want the truth about their numbers</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top surface" id="apply" aria-labelledby="apply-title">
  <div class="wrap apply">
    <div class="apply-copy">
      <h2 id="apply-title">Apply for your roadmap</h2>
      <p>Five answers. Then {% if funnel.bookingUrl %}you pick a time for a 30-minute call{% else %}Kevin emails you to set a 30-minute call{% endif %}, and he walks you through your roadmap. Then you decide whether you want us to do the work or to do it yourself.</p>
      {{ reviews(proof, ids=["google-brody-guy"]) }}
    </div>
    <form id="roadmap-form" class="form-grid" method="post" data-apply-form data-form-type="roadmap" data-endpoint="{{ funnel.applyEndpoint }}" data-booking-url="{{ funnel.bookingUrl }}" data-hcaptcha-sitekey="{{ funnel.hcaptchaSitekey or '' }}">
      <div class="field field-wide">
        <label for="rm-store">Store address</label>
        <input id="rm-store" name="store_url" type="text" inputmode="url" autocomplete="url" autocapitalize="none" spellcheck="false" maxlength="300" placeholder="yourbrand.com" aria-describedby="rm-store-error" required>
        <p class="field-error" id="rm-store-error" data-error-for="store_url" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="rm-revenue">Monthly online sales</label>
        <select id="rm-revenue" name="revenue_band" aria-describedby="rm-revenue-error" required>
          <option value="">Choose a range</option>
          {%- for band in funnel.revenue_bands %}
          <option value="{{ band.value }}">{{ band.label }}</option>
          {%- endfor %}
        </select>
        <p class="field-error" id="rm-revenue-error" data-error-for="revenue_band" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="rm-channel">Main sales channel</label>
        <select id="rm-channel" name="main_channel" aria-describedby="rm-channel-error" required>
          <option value="">Choose one</option>
          {%- for c in funnel.channels %}
          <option value="{{ c }}">{{ c }}</option>
          {%- endfor %}
        </select>
        <p class="field-error" id="rm-channel-error" data-error-for="main_channel" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="rm-role">Your role</label>
        <select id="rm-role" name="role" aria-describedby="rm-role-error" required>
          <option value="">Choose one</option>
          {%- for r in funnel.roles %}
          <option value="{{ r }}">{{ r }}</option>
          {%- endfor %}
        </select>
        <p class="field-error" id="rm-role-error" data-error-for="role" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="rm-email">Work email</label>
        <input id="rm-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false" maxlength="254" placeholder="you@yourbrand.com" aria-describedby="rm-email-error" required>
        <p class="field-error" id="rm-email-error" data-error-for="email" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
        <label for="rm-hp">Company URL (leave this empty)</label>
        <input id="rm-hp" name="hp_company_url" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
      </div>
      <div id="hcaptcha-slot" class="field-wide"></div>
      <div class="form-actions">
        <button type="submit" class="button button-primary" disabled>Send my application</button>
        <p class="helper">Free. You keep the roadmap either way.</p>
      </div>
      <noscript><p class="noscript-note field-wide">This form needs JavaScript. Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> instead and Kevin will reply.</p></noscript>
      <p class="helper field-wide">Form not working? <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Email {{ site.email }}</a>.</p>
      <div class="form-status" data-form-status tabindex="-1" hidden></div>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <h2 id="faq-title" class="split-head">Roadmap questions</h2>
    <div>{% include "partials/faq.njk" %}<p><a href="/faq/">More questions and answers</a></p><p class="helper">Not ready to apply? <a href="/free-business-audit/" data-cta="roadmap_site_check">Run the instant site check</a>. It is an automated scan of your site, not Kevin's read.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
